title: '[pallet-revive] Price storage deposit diffs before netting them'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/12692

    Storage deposit diffs netted added bytes and items against removed ones before applying a
    rate, so after `DepositPerByte` or `DepositPerChildTrieItem` was raised, replacing an item
    with one of the same size cost nothing. Additions are now charged at the current rate and
    removals refunded at the rate the contract paid, using exact integer arithmetic.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
